        "geology": "The soil consists of a deep (1.20?2.25 m) Aeolian cover sand layer (Dryas III), resting on a substratum of Clay of the Campine (> 40% of clay) (Tiglian) at variable depth, between 1.2 m and 2.5 m and more. ",
        "hydrology": "The soil is somewhat poorly drained, rarely saturated, but moist and with rapid hydraulic conductivity for all horizons. A perched water table is present at variable depth ranging between 0.8 and 2.5 m.",
        "soils": "The soil is characterized as a moderately wet and sandy arenosol with distinct horizons of humus and iron. pH(CaCl2) values ranges from 2.7 in the forest floor and increases from 3.1 at 5 cm of depth till 3.6 at 40-80 cm. Base saturation is lower than 10 % throughout the soil column. The C:N ratio of the FH layer was 30 whereas values in the mineral soil fell below 20. The forest floor is characterised as a mor-moder type.",
        "vegetation": "The forest stand in which the core plot is located is a Scots pine stand (Pinus sylvestris L.), which was planted in 1929 on former heathland. The herb layer is dominated by Molinia caerulea (L.) Moench and several ferns. The stand structure is further characterized by a diverse moss layer and ingrowth of several tree and shrub species (Betula pendula L., Frangula alnus Mill., Sorbus aucuparia L., ?)."
      },
